    "id": "youtube:5EGviuxqXiI",
    "source": "youtube",
    "type": "video",
    "title": "pitch modulation by using multiple auto-tune plugins at different rates",
    "text": "using two tuning plugins with different depth, detection range, and tuning speed can cause the pitch to jump around unexpectedly. detuning will amplify this effect.\n\na lot of width plugins will detune one side to manipulate the haas effect, which can also allow an autotune plugin later in the chain to do some interesting things to the pitch.\n\neffects chain (everything is free or stock):\n- melda autopitch (i use the width knob for haas effect here): https://www.meldaproduction.com/MAutoPitch\n- graillon 2: https://www.auburnsounds.com/products/Graillon.html\n- puberty simulator (formant shifting plugin): https://github.com/robbert-vdh/nih-plug/tree/master/plugins/puberty_simulator\n- airwindows density (saturation): https://www.airwindows.com/density\n- stock reverb with self-ducking from my last video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cPfXv2IQG0s\nand some more sidechain against the drums at the end",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5EGviuxqXiI",
